when you first look at biomutin in  action there's a sense that it's a  mashup of different fantasy and science  fiction genres  all vying for control described as a  post-apocalyptic kung fu  fable the action storytelling on display  presents an adventure that's an  intriguing mix  of the classic animated film secret of  nim along with the platforming and  action games like enslaved odyssey to  the west and  devil may cry and therein lies the hook  for by mutant  it wears its weirdness on its sleeve  presenting an alluring take on what the  post-apocalyptic earth  would look like once the animals inherit  the world before its full release on may  25th we had the chance to check out a  final preview of biomutant  we got a clearer sense of the game's  focus on action and storytelling and how  the hero's journey will evolve in a  world full of talking animals  and decaying automatons stories only  survive if someone is listening  so pay attention first revealed back in  2017  biomutant is the debut game from  experiment 101  a studio made up of the former  developers from the just core series  biomutant is a departure that instead  focuses on more exploring a  zelda-like map with action-rpg mechanics  that blend third-person combat and  rpg-like progression  while you may play as a nameless  protagonist biomutant's story is told  from the perspective of a narrator  who feels lifted from a children's  animated film however this works in  biomutant's favor  it presents a charming if unusual take  on a post-apocalyptic action rpg  where your narrative decisions and  tactics in combat are given commentary  from an omnipotent observer  this area is bio-contaminated  it's really hazardous the main plot  focuses on the hero's quest to save the  tree of life from rival clans  and an evil group known as the world  eaters who seek to trigger  a new apocalypse just before the intro  you can customize your hero's breed and  class types  along with their height fur colour and  some surprisingly robust options for  body proportions  define your genetic structure one of the  more intriguing details in biomutant is  its surprisingly robust crafting system  like its story in combat the crafting  element leans heavily into the  scavenging aspect of surviving  in the post-human world and all the  trinkets and scrap you find when  exploring the world  can be repurposed into new guns and  melee weapons one example we saw during  our preview was a new melee weapon  crafted from a walking cane  a pair of scissors and a mangled metal  safe door resulting in the kane  stronk box you can also add special  elemental modifiers to the mix  turning your jury rigged weapons into  death dealing machines  like the legend of zelda biomutant  features a mix of open exploration and  fast-paced  target locked combat when exploring the  different zones the hero character will  be able to leap  dash and rush across the large  landscapes and explore buildings to  scrounge supplies  and unearth clues about the planet's  ancient history on top of that they will  also be able to ride mounts made of  scrap  to explore the most dangerous areas of  the world including a toxic waterway  and heavily irradiated zones that  require you to constantly monitor your  health  we saw the broad strokes of what the  world is like during our look at the  game  and it's an incredibly detailed and  vibrant setting to see  however it still left me wondering about  the density of the game's apparently  eight by eight kilometer world  and how interconnected its locales will  all be in the final release  which was unfortunately difficult to get  a sense of in our preview  now the world is quite dangerous but the  hero character of biomutant comes with  an assortment of skills and weapons  to meet each challenge head on just like  in capcom's devil may cry your tactics  in combat focus on mixing melee strikes  with your firearms and special magic  attacks  which open up some clever opportunities  to hit enemies when they're most  vulnerable  but can sometimes come off as a bit  disorientating with a sudden shift  between third person and  lock-on targeting the number of options  you have can present some fun and  thrilling opportunities to finish a  fight in style  biomutant is balancing various mechanics  and approaches to storytelling  which certainly make for an enticing  take on a post-apocalyptic adventure  game this new open world  game has been a long time coming and  with its full release coming on may 25th  we're poised to see how this  post-apocalyptic kung fu fable  will unfold for more on biomutant and  other games releasing this summer  make sure to hit that subscribe button  and of course check on gamespot.com  [Music]  you
 

